# SEIS Second Brain Rule
- Treat `seis-brain/vault` as the public-safe Obsidian knowledge layer.
- Keep memory markdown-first and plain-text oriented.
- AI-generated second-brain items are draft until reviewed.
- Never turn the brain into random notes; keep explicit purpose, state, and next actions.
- Maintain index notes and context packs when adding major concepts.
- Preserve frontmatter for high-value notes (`type`, `module`, `status`, `visibility`, `updated`).
- Never include secrets, private data, or real host credentials in memory files.
